Title: Steam locomotive starts new journey in Sheringham
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Alex Alder', 'Text': 'After nine years of efforts, for the very first time ever she pulled passenger trains. It was absolutely incredible.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 40, 'EndChar': 160}}, {'Speaker': 'Mr Alder', 'Text': 'discovering the engine was like hearing "of a mythical Egyptian tomb".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 13, 'EndChar': 74}}, {'Speaker': 'Mr Alder', 'Text': 'I fully never expected to be driven down a Hertfordshire country lane, following a wild tip off about a lost engine.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 99}}, {'Speaker': 'Mr Alder', 'Text': "I could never have imagined taking tea and biscuits with [a] mother superior at a convent, and hearing of 'Malcolm's engine'.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 122}}, {'Speaker': 'Mr Alder', 'Text': 'But there it was in this convent in Hertfordshire, 39 tons of miracle,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 69}}, {'Speaker': 'Mr Alder', 'Text': 'it cost him about £200,000 to restore the locomotive, taking a team of volunteers about nine years to overhaul.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 12, 'EndChar': 114}}, {'Speaker': 'Graham Hukins', 'Text': 'it was "absolutely wonderful" to see the engine running in Sheringham.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 59, 'EndChar': 125}}, {'Speaker': 'Graham Hukins', 'Text': 'This weekend is the very first time it has been paired with passenger carriages, and it is an absolute delight to have it join our working fleet.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 1, 'EndChar': 139}}, {'Speaker': 'Graham Hukins', 'Text': 'to be part of that tale and to see her back in working order" was special as they celebrated 50-years of running trains at North Norfolk Railway.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 17, 'StartChar': 7, 'EndChar': 134}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'It re-entered service at the North Norfolk Railway in Sheringham on Saturday after a nine-year refurbishment.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 87}}, {'Description': 'North Norfolk Railway said it will use the engine to pull passenger carriages from Sheringham to Holt.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 88}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Four men, who are dressed in purple clothing, are standing in a row. Two are on the left and are standing outside of the locomotive, which is painted red and black with gold accents. Two men on the right are standing inside the locomotive. '}]}
